Z||000000||CUTTER||05-21-2000||08:24 PM||||I was comming home from carisle today and everytime i gave it gas and got around 75-80 MPH my front end would sway back and forth like I was steering it like that but I wasnt. I got blown away by a honda civic because of it. What could it be, also I have a vibrating sound comming from the tires. When I take turns it gets louder and sounds more harsh. Help!<P>Shane blue87GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||05-21-2000||09:02 PM||||Wheel bearings?||||reg||1
Z||000002||CUTTER||05-21-2000||09:06 PM||||Think the wheel bearings will cure both problems?||||reg||1
Z||000003||sully5||05-21-2000||09:39 PM||||What about the steering stabilizer? I have some severe bump steer problems and have been told that the stabilizer could be a big part of it. Just been to lazy to change it. Hope this helps some. Sully||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-21-2000||10:52 PM||||Low tire air pressure, Wheel alignment, Bad bearings, bent wheel, Unbalanced tires, These are just a few things that I can think of to check. If your tires are slightly worn they could be unbalanced. This would be noticable at high speeds. Also check the wheel weights if one fell off it could cause the same problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||CUTTER||05-21-2000||11:50 PM||||last week I just got new tires and got my front aligned. I think it might be bearings, but im not a expert or anywhere close so I need more advice, and so far so good!||||reg||1
